cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this tool in published work, please cite it below,
  alongside the underlying libraries it's built on (CRIM Intervals and
  music21 -- see this repo's README/in-app Credits section for those
  citations, and to cite a specific piece's own source collection).
type: software
title: "Renaissance Polyphony Research Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A Streamlit web app that aggregates ~4,300 Renaissance polyphony
  pieces from 7 sources (a music21-bundled corpus, CRIM Project,
  Josquin Research Project, 1520s Project, Tasso in Music Project,
  SEILS, Lassus's Geistliche Psalmen) into one searchable,
  analysis-ready place, and runs CRIM Intervals' structural analyses
  (cadences, points of imitation, homorhythm) on them, writing results
  back onto real notation, plotting them, or exporting them as data.
authors:
  - alias: "vclag"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vclag/Renaissance-score-workbench"
url: "https://renaissance-polyphony-research-toolkit.streamlit.app/"
date-released: "2026-08-29"
license: MIT
